cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this data or code, please cite both this repository
  (Zenodo DOI) and the paper.
title: 'Next-Generation Road Safety — companion data & code: exposure coverage autocorrelation and hot-spot validity in network crash mapping'
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Camargo
    given-names: Diego
    email: diegocamargo@cefetmg.br
    affiliation: Centro Federal de Educação Tecnológica de Minas Gerais (CEFET-MG)
repository-code: 'https://github.com/d-camargo/next-generation-road-safety'
abstract: >-
  Derived panel datasets, spatial statistics outputs, publication figures and
  the full replication pipeline for the study of exposure-coverage
  autocorrelation and hot-spot validity in network crash mapping on ten
  Brazilian federal corridors (2017-2025). Panel bins of 5/10/20 km keyed by
  (br, uf, km); crash counts from PRF open data (BAT); exposure from PNCT/DNIT
  annual AADT; global Moran and LISA with FDR local correction; conditional
  association and sampling-precision analyses. Data under CC-BY-4.0
  (LICENSE-DATA), code under MIT (LICENSE).
keywords:
  - road safety
  - spatial autocorrelation
  - exposure coverage
  - measurement error
  - Moran's I
  - LISA
  - empirical Bayes
  - Brazil
  - PRF
  - DNIT
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-10-05'
